    "a": "No. Dogs swallow toothpaste rather than spitting it out. Fluoride swallowed regularly can build up to toxic levels, and some toothpastes contain xylitol, which is dangerous to dogs even in small amounts. Use a toothpaste made for pets, or simply brush without toothpaste. The brushing itself is what cleans the teeth."
