    "q": "Are bones good for my dog's teeth?",
    "a": "Veterinary dentists advise against them. Bones, antlers and other hard chews commonly cause painful tooth fractures. If you can't bend or flex a chew, it's more likely to break a tooth. Choose softer, appropriately sized chews, and supervise your dog while they chew."
