  "faqs": [
   {
    "q": "My old dog can't stand for a bath. What are my options?",
    "a": "You have several options: Let your dog sit or lie down on a non-slip mat in the tub or shower. Support a larger dog with a padded harness when lifting them in and out. Spot-clean dirty patches with a pet spot cleaner or wipes between baths. Get help from a groomer or your vet's practice if a full bath at home isn't safe. If your dog seems to be in pain, see your vet first."
   },
   {
    "q": "Should I still brush a dog with thin skin?",
    "a": "Yes, gently. Brushing still helps keep the coat comfortable. Use a soft brush rather than one with stiff metal pins, which can be too harsh on thin skin and can nick warts or lumps. Keep sessions short, and check the skin as you go."
   },
   {
    "q": "My senior dog's coat isn't growing back after a clip. Should I worry?",
    "a": "Mention it to your vet. Coat that doesn't regrow, or new thinning or bald patches, is worth having checked rather than guessing at the cause."
   }
  ],
