  "faqs": [
   {
    "q": "Should I tip my dog groomer?",
    "a": "Tipping is your choice, not a requirement, and there's no official rule about how much. If you're not sure what's usual at a particular business, ask them. Repeat bookings and a good review are also appreciated."
   },
   {
    "q": "Can I stay with my dog while they're groomed?",
    "a": "It's reasonable to ask, especially the first time. Watching can show you how your dog copes, which is useful for future visits. But some dogs are more anxious when their owner is nearby, because they pick up on their owner's nerves. Policies vary between groomers, so ask when you book."
   },
   {
    "q": "Why was my dog shaved when I asked for a trim?",
    "a": "Usually because the coat was matted: Why it hurts: mats pull at the skin, and wet mats tighten as they dry. The kinder option: brushing out heavy matting can be painful for the dog, and clipping the coat short may be kinder. The coat will grow back. Avoiding a surprise: agree in advance what the groomer should do if they find mats, so you aren't caught out. To prevent mats between visits, see brushing and mats."
   }
  ],
